 ### Reference map
 
+The tables that follow state the value the cascade declares for each token, and
+`tests/src/styles/tokens.test.ts` resolves every stated value against the built cascade in each
+mode. A value cell states its values as one code span for each token the row's first cell names, as
+`` `light`, dark `dark` `` where a table's single value column carries both modes, or as `the same
+expression` where the dark scope repeats the light cell. A cell written in any other form describes
+a scale or a law instead of stating a value, and the case that reads that scale is what proves it. A
+`Role` cell names the role whose fill the row gives, so that row's token is the role's own
+`--vn-color-{role}-base`. A `Tier` row is a template over `{role}` and `{fill}`, and it expands over
+every role the preceding table names.
+
+The styles build shortens a number and a duration, so a stated value and the declaration are
+compared with every number written in full and every millisecond duration written in seconds. The
+build also rewrites a color channel into the engine's own serialization, so a pair that differs as
+text is compared again as the color each side paints.
+
 #### Factors
 
